{% block content %}

<section class="panorama panorama--solo" id="section-a" aria-label="Hero">
  <div class="panorama__hero">
    <h1 class="display">make your product<br>make sense<span class="end">.</span></h1>

    <p class="lede">
      We turn complex product ideas into clear journeys, screens, and requirements. Your team gets a Design Plan to build from.
    </p>

    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="hero-cta" href="#section-d">Start a conversation</a>
      <a class="forward-cue" href="#method-pipeline">How we work</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-block" id="section-plan" aria-labelledby="plan-heading">
<h2 class="home-block__title" id="plan-heading">a plan you can build from.</h2>
<p class="home-block__body">For a new product or a redesign, the first engagement delivers a Design Plan. Review the direction before committing to production.</p>
<ul class="home-list">
<li><strong>The product map.</strong> What people manage, how those things connect, and what people can do with them.</li>
<li><strong>The key journeys and wireframes.</strong> How someone moves through the work, including what happens when things go wrong.</li>
<li><strong>The requirements and validation plan.</strong> What to build and what still needs to be tested.</li>
</ul>
<p class="home-block__body" style="margin-top:24px">Build with your team, or scope a separate build with us once the plan is accepted.</p>
</section>

<section class="process-timeline" id="method-pipeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title"><header class="timeline-heading"><span class="timeline-kicker">OUR APPROACH</span><h2 id="timeline-title">from context to a clear screen.</h2><p>Take something familiar: ordering a coffee. Follow one oat latte from the first conversation to an order screen.</p></header><ol class="timeline-steps"><li class="timeline-step"><span class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div class="timeline-copy"><h3>understand the work.</h3><p>We start with what a person wants to do. Here, a customer wants to order their coffee ahead, and the café needs the details to make it.</p></div><figure class="timeline-illustration"><div class="context-notes"><blockquote><span class="note-label">THE CUSTOMER</span><p>“One medium oat latte, please. I’d like to pick it up on my way to work.”</p></blockquote><blockquote><span class="note-label">THE CAFÉ</span><p>“People choose a drink, a size, and a milk. An order can include several drinks.”</p></blockquote></div></figure></li><li class="timeline-step"><span class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="timeline-copy"><h3>find the pieces.</h3><p>We identify what people choose, what they need to know, and what they can do. A latte on the menu is different from the oat latte in someone’s order.</p></div><figure class="timeline-illustration"><div class="word-sort"><div><h4>Things people choose and track</h4><p><span class="word-chip word-chip--object">drink</span><span class="word-chip word-chip--object">order item</span><span class="word-chip word-chip--object">order</span></p></div><div><h4>Information they need</h4><p><span class="word-chip">size</span><span class="word-chip">milk</span><span class="word-chip">quantity</span><span class="word-chip">price</span><span class="word-chip">pickup estimate</span></p></div><div><h4>Actions they take</h4><p><span class="word-chip word-chip--action">choose a drink</span><span class="word-chip word-chip--action">customize</span><span class="word-chip word-chip--action">add to order</span><span class="word-chip word-chip--action">place order</span></p></div></div></figure></li><li class="timeline-step"><span class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="timeline-copy"><h3>give each piece a place.</h3><p>The drink defines the available choices. The order item records the customer’s size, milk, and quantity. The order holds the total and pickup details.</p></div><figure class="timeline-illustration"><table class="object-matrix"><caption class="visually-hidden">Coffee ordering: drink, order item, and order, with their information and actions.</caption><thead><tr><td></td><th scope="col">drink</th><th scope="col">order item</th><th scope="col">order</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Information</th><td><span>name</span><span>available options</span><span>base price</span></td><td><span>size</span><span>milk</span><span>quantity</span><span>item total</span></td><td><span>pickup estimate</span><span>total</span><span>status</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Actions</th><td><span>choose</span></td><td><span>customize</span><span>remove</span></td><td><span>place order</span></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="mobile-matrix"><section class="mobile-object"><h3>drink</h3><dl><div><dt>Information</dt><dd><span>name</span><span>available options</span><span>base price</span></dd></div><div><dt>Actions</dt><dd><span>choose</span></dd></div></dl></section><section class="mobile-object"><h3>order item</h3><dl><div><dt>Information</dt><dd><span>size</span><span>milk</span><span>quantity</span><span>item total</span></dd></div><div><dt>Actions</dt><dd><span>customize</span><span>remove</span></dd></div></dl></section><section class="mobile-object"><h3>order</h3><dl><div><dt>Information</dt><dd><span>pickup estimate</span><span>total</span><span>status</span></dd></div><div><dt>Actions</dt><dd><span>place order</span></dd></div></dl></section></div></figure></li><li class="timeline-step"><span class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div class="timeline-copy"><h3>connect the objects.</h3><p>One order can contain several items. Each item refers to a drink on the menu, with the customer’s choices attached.</p></div><figure class="timeline-illustration"><div class="relationship-map"><div class="relationship-node"><span class="diagram-label">THE PURCHASE</span><strong>order</strong><small>#1042 · pickup</small></div><div class="relationship-edge"><span>contains</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></div><div class="relationship-node relationship-node--focus"><span class="diagram-label">YOUR CHOICE</span><strong>order item</strong><small>Medium · oat milk · ×1</small></div><div class="relationship-edge"><span>refers to</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></div><div class="relationship-node"><span class="diagram-label">ON THE MENU</span><strong>drink</strong><small>Latte</small></div></div></figure></li><li class="timeline-step"><span class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true">05</span><div class="timeline-copy"><h3>choose what matters.</h3><p>Before placing an order, the customer needs to confirm their coffee, see the price, and know when to collect it. Those questions set the screen’s priorities.</p></div><figure class="timeline-illustration"><div class="task-brief"><div class="task-brief__head"><span class="diagram-label">ORDERING AHEAD</span><h4>“Can I get my oat latte<br>and know when it’ll be ready?”</h4></div><dl><div><dt>Confirm</dt><dd>Drink, size, milk, and quantity</dd></div><div><dt>Show clearly</dt><dd>Total price and pickup estimate</dd></div><div><dt>Primary action</dt><dd>Place order <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></dd></div></dl></div></figure></li><li class="timeline-step"><span class="timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true">06</span><div class="timeline-copy"><h3>shape the screen.</h3><p>The wireframe brings those decisions together: the configured coffee, the order total, the pickup estimate, and one clear action to place the order.</p></div><figure class="timeline-illustration"><div class="coffee-wireframe"><header><span>morning coffee<span class="app-period">.</span></span><span class="diagram-label">PICKUP ORDER</span></header><div class="coffee-order"><div class="coffee-order__heading"><h4>your order.</h4><span>1 item</span></div><div class="coffee-item"><div class="coffee-cup" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 80 90"><path d="M19 27h42l-5 48H24zM16 20h48v7H16zM23 13h34l4 7H19zM22 43h36M25 59h31"/></svg></div><div class="coffee-item__details"><span class="diagram-label">DRINK</span><h5>Oat latte</h5><dl><div><dt>Size</dt><dd>Medium</dd></div><div><dt>Milk</dt><dd>Oat</dd></div><div><dt>Quantity</dt><dd>1</dd></div></dl></div><strong class="coffee-price">$5.50</strong></div><div class="coffee-pickup"><span class="diagram-label">PICKUP ESTIMATE</span><strong>Ready in 5–8 minutes</strong></div><div class="coffee-total"><span>Total</span><strong>$5.50</strong></div><span class="coffee-place-order">Place order <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></div></figure></li></ol></section>
<section class="plan-gallery" id="design-plans" aria-labelledby="gallery-heading"><header><h2 id="gallery-heading">see what a design plan looks like.</h2><p>Three example plans, from the initial problem to the screens and requirements.</p></header><div class="plan-gallery-grid">{% for plan in designPlans %}<article class="plan-card"><a href="{{ ('/design-plans/' + plan.slug + '/') | url }}"><img src="{{ plan.previewImage | url }}" width="800" height="620" alt="{{ plan.previewAlt | escape }}" loading="lazy"><div class="plan-card-body"><h3>{{ plan.name }}</h3><p>{{ plan.summary }}</p><span class="plan-card-link">View Design Plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></div></a></article>{% endfor %}</div></section>

